  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an integer KKK, consider an array AAA of size NNN. You can perform the following operation on the array:\n\n\nSelect an integer XXX;\nRemove all elements from AAA satisfying X≤Ai&lt;X+KX \\le A_i \\lt X + KX≤Ai​&lt;X+K.\nLet f(A)f(A)f(A) denote the **minimum** number of such operations needed to make the array AAA empty, i.e. delete all of its elements.\n\nGiven integers NNN and MMM, find the sum of f(A)f(A)f(A) over all **strictly increasing** arrays AAA of **size NNN** satisfying 1≤Ai≤M1 \\le A_i \\le M1≤Ai​≤M.\n\nSince the answer may be large, output it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three space-separated integers, NNN, MMM and KKK, as mentioned in the statement.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the required sum of minimum operations of all such arrays modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1041 \\le T \\le 3 \\cdot 10^41≤T≤3⋅104",
      "1≤N,K≤M≤1061 \\le N, K \\le M \\le 10^61≤N,K≤M≤106",
      "The sum of MMM over all test cases doesn't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n4 5 1\n2 3 2\n3 4 2\n3 4 3\n100 200 100",
        "output": "20\n4\n8\n6\n814673489",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Since K=1K = 1K=1, each operation can delete atmost 111 element, thus clearly we need NNN operations per array, and there are 555 arrays, hence the answer is 5⋅4=205 \\cdot 4 = 205⋅4=20.\nTest case 222: There are 333 possible arrays :\n\n[1,2][1, 2][1,2] : We use one operation with X=1X = 1X=1, thus f([1,2])=1f([1, 2]) = 1f([1,2])=1.\n[2,3][2, 3][2,3] : We use one operation with X=2X = 2X=2, thus f([2,3])=1f([2, 3]) = 1f([2,3])=1.\n[1,3][1, 3][1,3] : We must use at least 222 operations, and we can do that by first choosing X=1X = 1X=1 and then X=2X = 2X=2, thus f([1,3])=2f([1, 3]) = 2f([1,3])=2.\n\nThus, sum of f(A)f(A)f(A) is 444."
      }
    ]
  },
